As you can tell, a lot of overlaps. Lets pick a few signatures of interest from across this gradient. 


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true"}
Representative <- TheSignatures |> dplyr::filter(
    Cluster %in% c("B9_10-YG6_07-V13_07", "B9_10-YG6_07-V13_06",
     "Average", "B9_10-YG6_05-V13_05")) |> rename(Fluorophore=Cluster)
```
:::


![](images/RepresentativePerCPCy55.png)

And checking quickly the cosine similarity, we find that despite visual difference, they all still are relatively close to each other compared to the APC-Fire 810 signatures. This is partly due to the extra autofluorescent peaks only making up a minor contribution to the overall area under the signature curve for the overall fluorophore peaks. 


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true"}
Luciernaga_Cosine(data=Representative, colorlow="lightblue",
 limitlow=0.9)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](index_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-50-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::


To keep things organized, lets place everything into its own subfolder. 


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true"}
StashHere <- file.path(OutputLocation, "IteratedPerCP-Cy55")

if (!dir.exists(StashHere)){dir.create(StashHere)}

SignatureVariants <- Representative |> pull(Fluorophore)
```
:::


Then carry out iterative unmixing for the respective signature variants. 


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true"}
walk(.x=SignatureVariants, .f=IteratedUnmix, fcs_files=fcs_files,
 AlternateMatrix = Representative, SignatureMatrix = UpdatedSignatureMatrix,
 outpath = StashHere,ThisFluorophore = "PerCP-Cy5.5")
```
:::


Read these .fcs files back in, and generate the corresponding visuals


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true"}
TheseFCSFiles <- list.files(StashHere, pattern=".fcs", full.names=TRUE)
TheCytoset <- load_cytoset_from_fcs(TheseFCSFiles,
 truncate_max_range=FALSE, transformation=FALSE)
TheGatingSet <- GatingSet(TheCytoset)

SFC_Parameters <- colnames(TheGatingSet)
FluorophoresOnly <- SFC_Parameters[!stringr::str_detect(SFC_Parameters, "FSC|SSC|Time")]
Biexponential <-  flowjo_biexp_trans(channelRange=4096,
 maxValue=4194304, pos=5.62, neg=0, widthBasis=-1000)
MyBiexTransform <- transformerList(FluorophoresOnly, Biexponential)
transform(TheGatingSet, MyBiexTransform)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
A GatingSet with 16 samples
```


:::
:::



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true"}
IterateThroughTheseColumns <- FluorophoresOnly [!stringr::str_detect(FluorophoresOnly, "PerCP")]

AssembledPlots <- map(.x= IterateThroughTheseColumns,
 .f=Utility_UnityPlot, y="PerCP-Cy5.5-A", GatingSet=TheGatingSet,
 sample.name="GUID", bins=120, removestrings="_Unmixed.fcs",
 marginsubset="root", gatesubset="root", returntype="patchwork",
 reference=NULL, clearance=0.2, gatelines=FALSE, therows=2, thecolumns=2)
```
:::


Before saving to a .pdf


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true"}
Utility_Patchwork(x=AssembledPlots, filename="IteratedPerCPCy5.5",
 outfolder=StashHere, thecolumns=1, therows=1, NotListofList = FALSE,
 patches=TRUE)
```
:::


Lets save the cell-derrived signature with the less autofluorescence contributions, and update the signature matrix. 


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true"}
AlternateMatrix <- Representative
SignatureMatrix <- AssembledSignatures
ThisFluorophore <- "PerCP-Cy5.5"
ThisVariant <- "B9_10-YG6_05-V13_05"

UpdatedSignatureMatrix2 <- UpdatedSignatureMatrix |>
    dplyr::rows_update(
        AlternateMatrix |>
        dplyr::filter(Fluorophore %in% ThisVariant) |>
        dplyr::mutate(Fluorophore = ThisFluorophore),
        by = "Fluorophore"
    )

# UpdatedSignatureMatrix2 |> View()
```
:::


At which point, we can repeat the generation of the hotspot matrices, and the change between them matrix plot



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true"}
OldHotspot <- Hotspots(data=UpdatedSignatureMatrix,
 fileName="OriginalPerCPCy55",
 outpath = StashHere,
 returnType="plot")
```
:::


![](/course/15_EvaluatingUnmixing/outputs/IteratedPerCP-Cy55/OriginalPerCPCy55.png)


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true"}
UpdatedHotspot <- Hotspots(data=UpdatedSignatureMatrix2,
 fileName="UpdatedPerCPCy55",
 outpath = StashHere,
 returnType="plot")
```
:::


![](/course/15_EvaluatingUnmixing/outputs/IteratedPerCP-Cy55/UpdatedPerCPCy55.png)


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true"}
OldHotspot <- Hotspots(data=UpdatedSignatureMatrix,
 fileName="OriginalPerCPCy55",
 outpath = StashHere,
 returnType="data")

UpdatedHotspot <- Hotspots(data=UpdatedSignatureMatrix2,
 fileName="UpdatedPerCPCy55",
 outpath = StashHere,
 returnType="data")

HotspotDifference(HotspotBrighter=OldHotspot,
 HotspotDimmer=UpdatedHotspot, outpath=StashHere,
 fileName = "Difference_PerCPCy55")
```
:::


![](/course/15_EvaluatingUnmixing/outputs/IteratedPerCP-Cy55/Difference_PerCPCy55.png)

Overall, looking at the difference plot, switching out this signature variant does not appear to have made any substantial differences across most fluorophores, with most of the difference values being less than 0.3. When we open IteratedPerCPCy5.5 on these values, the changes also appear to be relatively minor, as can be seen in the following example:

![](images/PerCP_Nada.png)

So in this case, while switching the signature didn't hurt, it certainly didn't appear to help all that much, at least for the moment. 

### BV421

Moving on from the limited changes from switching out PerCP-Cy5.5, lets check on BV421. 

![](images/5_BV421.png)


From the [Luciernaga](/course/SDY3080/LuciernagaIntegration.qmd) run, all signature variants came back across the board as having the V3-A as their peak detector. This is a little odd, given that the main reference signature is supposed to be V1-A based on the reference. 

![](images/NextUp_BV421.png)

Whether this small difference is due to the instrument, or changes in the vial due to something the manufacturer did, is a different investigation. For now, since its consistent across the board, lets see what we can do to provide a representative signature that has less autofluorescence residuals present. 

As was the case for the above, load in the signature variants


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true"}
TheCSV <- csv_files[stringr::str_detect(csv_files, "BV421")]
TheSignatures <- read.csv(TheCSV, check.names=FALSE)

Plot <- VisualizeSignatures(data=TheSignatures, columnname="Cluster")
```
:::



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true"}
plotly::ggplotly(Plot)
```

